(ARG-38 — the Practical Pattern example (LANGUAGE.md:4867-4879),
 verbatim, including the two quoted flag names: `'version'` and
 `'number'` are only legal because they are quoted — both are reserved
 words unquoted.
 Also covers: ARG-39 (a boolean flag's own name used bare as an If
 condition, with no comparison) and ARG-40 (`Print each item from
 arguments's all` prints each positional argument, one per line).
